###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168518
gdsn:cv168518 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-778930468 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "DTB (fashion) Dialog Textil – Bekleiding (DTB) a German group of companies who joined forces for the TC sector. The product classification can be found on their website http://www.dialog-dtb.de if you are a member." ;
              rdfs:label "47" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168518" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168519
gdsn:cv168519 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-778930468 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "SGI-DHO (Sporting Goods Industry Data Harmonization Organization) is representing the interests of the different stakeholders of the sporting goods industry (retailers + brands). Its main task is the development and harmonisation of codes, which can be used by the sporting goods industry to exchange and analyse data. The focus is set on codes that have not already been standardised by international trade organisations. In addition to the FEDAS (the European Federation of Sporting Goods Retail Associations) product classification key that has been developed a few years ago, and which is used by may stakeholders of the sporting goods industry, SGI-DHO is working on various other codes. Under www.sgidho.com you can find further information." ;
              rdfs:label "48" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168519" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168520
gdsn:cv168520 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-778930468 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "EAS (footwear) European Article System: A harmonised system to classify and process the characteristics of shoes across Europe." ;
              rdfs:label "49" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168520" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168521
gdsn:cv168521 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-778930468 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "United Nations Standard Products and Services Code" ;
              rdfs:label "5" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168521" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168522
gdsn:cv168522 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-778930468 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The Australian Therapeutic Goods Administration (TGA) classifies products it authorizes for sale in Australia. These items are considered either: Registered, Listed, Included or Classified as Other on the Australia Register of Therapeutic Goods (ARTG)." ;
              rdfs:label "50" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168522" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168523
gdsn:cv168523 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-778930468 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "SUSMP: An Australian classification and labelling of drugs and poisons named the Standard for the Uniform Scheduling of Medicines and Poisons (SUSMP). This was created and is maintained by the National Drugs and Poisons Scheduling Committee (NDPSC) which operates under control of the Therapeutic Goods Administration (TGA). This standard contains a list of 'Schedules', which are a way of grouping products together that may have similar regulatory controls over their availability. Criteria for scheduling may include such considerations as the purpose of use, potential for abuse, safety of use and the level of need for it." ;
              rdfs:label "51" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168523" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168524
gdsn:cv168524 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-778930468 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "In Australia, medicine may be subsidized by its Government via the Pharmaceutical Benefits Scheme (PBS). The PBS is a program available to all Australian residents covered under the public healthcare system (known as Medicare). The Pharmaceutical Benefits Schedule lists all drugs available under the scheme and the conditions under which it may be used. The PBS is a way of the Australian government subsidising the cost of particular medicines to make them more affordable for the community. E.g. A consumer is entitled to purchase 100 tablets of aspirin under the scheme, the retail cost is $13.00, the government subsidizes $9.50, so the consumer will pay the difference of $3.50 for the medication. The Repatriation Pharmaceutical Benefits Scheme is effectively the same scheme, however, offered to eligible war veterans, war widows and their dependents." ;
              rdfs:label "52" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168524" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168525
gdsn:cv168525 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-778930468 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The Therapeutic Goods Administration (TGA) have their own classification system for medical devices within Healthcare. The purpose of this classification is to ascertain the potential risk of a device through analysing the intended purpose of the product and using a set of classification rules. This classification allows the regulator to determine how much intervention is required before the device becomes available on the market." ;
              rdfs:label "53" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168525" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168526
gdsn:cv168526 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-778930468 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Milch Industrie Verband Cheese Class association of the German Dairy." ;
              rdfs:label "54" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168526" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168527
gdsn:cv168527 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-778930468 ;
