              rdfs:comment "Bitter beers are characterized by a distinct bitterness, and of which the colour can vary from golden blond to dark amber." ;
              rdfs:label "BEER_ALE_BITTER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AlcoholBeverageTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168789" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168790
gdsn:cv168790 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1001786865 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Bock is a bottom fermenting lager and typically spends extra time in cold storage during the winter months to smooth the intense flavours that develop during the brewing process. Stronger than a typical lager, bock is dark amber in colour with robust malt flavours and very light hoppiness." ;
              rdfs:label "BEER_BOCK" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AlcoholBeverageTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168790" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168791
gdsn:cv168791 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1001786865 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "IPAs (short for India pale ales) boast strong hop bitterness with piney and floral flavours. These beers also have high alcohol content." ;
              rdfs:label "BEER_INDIA_PALE_ALE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AlcoholBeverageTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168791" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168792
gdsn:cv168792 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1001786865 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Lager beers are made with bottom-fermenting yeast. Because the Lager yeast works at low temperatures, it converts the sugars very slowly into alcohol without leaving many traces. The taste of the beer therefore comes almost entirely from the grains and hops." ;
              rdfs:label "BEER_LAGER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AlcoholBeverageTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168792" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168793
gdsn:cv168793 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1001786865 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The alcohol product is a Beer which is not otherwise enumerated in this codeset" ;
              rdfs:label "BEER_OTHER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AlcoholBeverageTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168793" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168794
gdsn:cv168794 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1001786865 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Sour beer is typically very low in alcohol, and feature tart, sour flavours that come from (safe) bacteria in the brew mash." ;
              rdfs:label "BEER_SOUR" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AlcoholBeverageTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168794" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168795
gdsn:cv168795 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1001786865 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Stout and Porter are both malty beers of dark malt, dark in colour, in both a lot of hops is used, and both have a thick creamy, firm mocha coloured foam head." ;
              rdfs:label "BEER_STOUT_PORTER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AlcoholBeverageTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168795" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168796
gdsn:cv168796 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1001786865 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Wheat beers use wheat as their malt. They are generally lighter in colour and alcohol content. Their tangy flavours go great with fruit, and brewers often add seasonal fruits to wheat beer." ;
              rdfs:label "BEER_WHEAT_BEER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AlcoholBeverageTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168796" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168797
gdsn:cv168797 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1001786865 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Beer, flavoured with spirit, fruit, herbs or other flavourings, after the fermentation." ;
              rdfs:label "FLAVOURED_BEER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AlcoholBeverageTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168797" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168798
gdsn:cv168798 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1001786865 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Ice wine is a type of dessert wine produced from grapes that have been frozen while still on the vine which has been fortified with a distilled spirit, usually Brandy." ;
              rdfs:label "FORTIFIED_WINE_ICE_WINE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AlcoholBeverageTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168798" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168799
gdsn:cv168799 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1001786865 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Madeira is a fortified wine made on the Portuguese Madeira Islands, off the coast of Africa. Madeira is produced in a variety of styles ranging from dry wines which can be consumed on their own as an aperitif to sweet wines usually consumed with dessert." ;
              rdfs:label "FORTIFIED_WINE_MADEIRA" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AlcoholBeverageTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168799" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv168800
gdsn:cv168800 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1001786865 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Malaga is a sweet fortified wine originating in the Spanish city of Málaga made from Pedro Ximénez and Moscatel grapes." ;
              rdfs:label "FORTIFIED_WINE_MALAGA" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "AlcoholBeverageTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "168800" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


