                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "German Style Pilsners are made with neutral and hard water. They tend to be golden in colour with a dry, crisp, and somewhat bitter flavour. Pilsner stands out from other lagers due to its more distinctive hop taste." ;
              rdfs:label "GERMAN_STYLE_PILSNER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169883" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169884
gdsn:cv169884 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "German Style Rye beer refers to any beer, crafted originally in Germany, in which rye (generally malted) is substituted for some portion of the barley. Rye beers are considered specialty beers that are brewed with unusual fermentables such as rice, corn, or wheat." ;
              rdfs:label "GERMAN_STYLE_RYE_ALE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169884" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169885
gdsn:cv169885 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "German Style Schwarzbier, or black beer, is a dark lager, crafted originally in Germany, which tend to have an opaque, black colour with hints of chocolate or coffee flavours, and are generally around 5% ABV. They are similar to stout in that they are made from roasted malt, which gives them their dark colour." ;
              rdfs:label "GERMAN_STYLE_SCHWARZBIER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169885" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169886
gdsn:cv169886 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Golden or Blonde ales are very pale in colour and tend to be clear, crisp, and dry, with low to medium bitterness and aroma from hops, and some sweetness from malt." ;
              rdfs:label "GOLDEN_OR_BLONDE_ALE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169886" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169887
gdsn:cv169887 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Gose is a warm fermented beer usually brewed with at least 50% of the grain bill being malted wheat. Dominant flavours in gose include a lemon sourness, a herbal characteristic, and a strong saltiness. Gose beers typically do not have prominent hop bitterness, flavours, or aroma. The beers typically have a moderate alcohol content of 4 to 5% ABV." ;
              rdfs:label "GOSE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169887" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169888
gdsn:cv169888 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Gueuze is a type of Lambic beer. It is made by blending young (1 year old) and old (2 to 3 year old) Lambic, which is bottled for a second fermentation. Because the young Lambic are not fully fermented, the blended beer contains fermentable sugars, which allow a second fermentation to occur." ;
              rdfs:label "GUEUZE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169888" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169889
gdsn:cv169889 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A strong, bottom-fermented spring beer, and one designed to bridge the chasm from hearty wintry brews to bright summer fare." ;
              rdfs:label "HELLES_BOCK" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169889" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169890
gdsn:cv169890 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "An herb and spice beer is a lager or ale that contains flavours derived from flowers, roots, seeds or certain fruits or vegetables. Typically the hop character is low, allowing the added ingredient to shine through. The appearance, mouthfeel and aromas vary depending on the herb or spice used. This beer style encompasses innovative examples as well as traditional holiday and winter ales." ;
              rdfs:label "HERB_AND_SPICE_BEER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169890" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169891
gdsn:cv169891 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A full-bodied beer with a creamy texture and copper colour. Honey beers are slightly sweet with hints of caramel." ;
              rdfs:label "HONEY" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169891" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169892
gdsn:cv169892 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Imperial or Double India Pale Ale is a style of pale ale. They are a stronger, very hoppy variant of IPAs." ;
              rdfs:label "IMPERIAL_OR_DOUBLE_INDIA_PALE_ALE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169892" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169893
gdsn:cv169893 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Imperial Red Ale is a beer ranging from amber to deep crimson in colour, with a robust, sweet, toasted malt character that is balanced by a bold, pronounced hop profile." ;
              rdfs:label "IMPERIAL_RED_ALE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169893" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169894
gdsn:cv169894 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Imperial stout is a strong dark beer. Imperial stouts have a high alcohol content, usually over 9% abv, and are among the darkest available beer styles." ;
              rdfs:label "IMPERIAL_STOUT" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169894" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169895
gdsn:cv169895 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "International Style Pale ale is a top fermented beer, crafted from various recipes around the world, made with predominantly pale malt. The highest proportion of pale malts results in a lighter colour." ;
              rdfs:label "INTERNATIONAL_STYLE_PALE_ALE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169895" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169896
gdsn:cv169896 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "International Style Pale lager is a top fermented beer, crafted from various recipes around the world, made with predominantly pale malt. The highest proportion of pale malts results in a lighter colour." ;
              rdfs:label "INTERNATIONAL_STYLE_PALE_LAGER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169896" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169897
gdsn:cv169897 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "International Style Pilsners are made with neutral and hard water. They tend to be golden in colour with a dry, crisp, and somewhat bitter flavour. Pilsner stands out from other lagers due to its more distinctive hop taste." ;
              rdfs:label "INTERNATIONAL_STYLE_PILSNER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169897" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169898
gdsn:cv169898 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Dry stout are stout beers which are less sweet than other stout beers." ;
              rdfs:label "IRISH_STYLE_DRY_STOUT" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169898" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169899
gdsn:cv169899 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Extra Stout is a dark, top-fermented beer which are stronger than traditional stout beers." ;
              rdfs:label "IRISH_STYLE_EXTRA_STOUT" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169899" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169900
gdsn:cv169900 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Irish red ale, red ale, or Irish ale is a name used by brewers in Ireland." ;
              rdfs:label "IRISH_STYLE_RED_ALE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169900" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169901
gdsn:cv169901 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Irish Style stout is a dark, top fermented beer, crafted originally in Irish, with a number of variations, including dry stout, Baltic porter, milk stout, and imperial stout." ;
              rdfs:label "IRISH_STYLE_STOUT" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169901" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169902
gdsn:cv169902 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Kölsch is a style of beer with an original gravity between 11 and 16 degrees Plato (specific gravity of 1.044 to 1.065)." ;
              rdfs:label "KOELSCH" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169902" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169903
gdsn:cv169903 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Lambic beers include gueuze and kriek Lambic. Lambic differs from most other beers in that it is fermented through exposure to wild yeasts and bacteria, as opposed to exposure to carefully cultivated strains of brewer's yeast. This process gives the beer its distinctive flavour: dry, vinous, and cidery, usually with a sour aftertaste." ;
              rdfs:label "LAMBIC" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169903" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169904
gdsn:cv169904 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Leipzig-Style Gose is a warm fermented beer that originated in Goslar, Germany. It is usually brewed with at least 50% of the grain bill being malted wheat. Dominant flavours in gose include a lemon sourness, an herbal characteristic, and a strong saltiness (the result of either local water sources or added salt). Gose beers typically do not have prominent hop bitterness, flavours, or aroma." ;
              rdfs:label "LEIPZIG_STYLE_GOSE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169904" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169905
gdsn:cv169905 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Typically light in flavour with a refreshing lime taste. The intensity of the lime can differ from very subtle to strong." ;
              rdfs:label "LIME" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169905" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169906
gdsn:cv169906 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Märzen or Märzenbier is a lager with a medium to full body and may vary in colour from pale through amber to dark brown." ;
              rdfs:label "MAERZEN" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169906" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169907
gdsn:cv169907 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Mixed Culture Brett beers vary in colour and can take on the hues of added fruits or other ingredients. Horsey, goaty, leathery, phenolic and some fruity acidic character derived from a mixed variety of Brettanomyces organisms may be evident, but in balance with other components of a Brett beer." ;
              rdfs:label "MIXED_CULTURE_BRETT_BEER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169907" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169908
gdsn:cv169908 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Dunkel, or Dunkles, is a word used for several types of dark German lager. Dunkel is the German word meaning dark, and Dunkel beers typically range in colour from amber to dark reddish brown. They are characterized by their smooth malty flavour." ;
              rdfs:label "MUENCHNER_MUNICH_STYLE_DUNKEL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169908" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169909
gdsn:cv169909 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Helles or Hell is a traditional German pale lager beer, produced chiefly in Southern Germany, particularly Munich." ;
              rdfs:label "MUENCHNER_MUNICH_STYLE_HELLES" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169909" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169910
gdsn:cv169910 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Stout is a dark, top-fermented beer with a number of variations, including dry stout, Baltic porter, milk stout, and imperial stout. Oatmeal stout is a stout with a proportion of oats, normally a maximum of 30%, added during the brewing process." ;
              rdfs:label "OATMEAL_STOUT" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169910" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169911
gdsn:cv169911 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Old ale is a term commonly applied to dark, malty beers in England, generally above 5% ABV, also to dark ales of any strength in Australia" ;
              rdfs:label "OLD_ALE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169911" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169912
gdsn:cv169912 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Ordinary Bitter is a variation of a British style of pale ale that varies in colour from gold to dark amber, and in strength typically from 3% to 5.5% alcohol by volume." ;
              rdfs:label "ORDINARY_BITTER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169912" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169913
gdsn:cv169913 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Oud Bruin, is a style of sour ale fermented with organisms other than Saccharomyces cerevisiae, especially Lactobacillus, which produces a sour character attributable to lactic acid." ;
              rdfs:label "OUD_BRUIN" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169913" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169914
gdsn:cv169914 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Perhaps the most seasonal of seasonal beers, the Pumpkin Spice beer style is brewed with pumpkin spices. Since the fruit does not have much of a taste by itself, many craft brewers have taken to adding spices typically found in pumpkin pie, like cinnamon and clove." ;
              rdfs:label "PUMPKIN_SPICE_BEER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169914" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169915
gdsn:cv169915 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Perhaps the most seasonal of seasonal beers, the Pumpkin/Squash beer style can be brewed with pumpkin or even winter squash. Since the fruit does not have much of a taste by itself, many craft brewers have taken to adding spices typically found in pumpkin pie, like cinnamon and clove." ;
              rdfs:label "PUMPKIN_SQUASH_BEER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169915" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169916
gdsn:cv169916 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Robust porter is a dark style of beer from well-hopped beers made from brown malt." ;
              rdfs:label "ROBUST_PORTER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169916" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169917
gdsn:cv169917 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Rye beer refers to any beer in which rye (generally malted) is substituted for some portion of the barley. Rye beers are considered specialty beers that are brewed with unusual fermentables such as rice, corn, or wheat." ;
              rdfs:label "RYE_BEER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169917" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169918
gdsn:cv169918 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Saison is a pale ale that is highly carbonated, fruity, spicy, and often bottle conditioned." ;
              rdfs:label "SAISON" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169918" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169919
gdsn:cv169919 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Schwarzbier, or black beer, is a dark lager which tend to have an opaque, black colour with hints of chocolate or coffee flavours, and are generally around 5% ABV. They are similar to stout in that they are made from roasted malt, which gives them their dark colour." ;
              rdfs:label "SCHWARZBIER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169919" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169920
gdsn:cv169920 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Scotch ale tends toward sweetness from residual sugars, malty notes, and a full body." ;
              rdfs:label "SCOTCH_ALE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169920" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169921
gdsn:cv169921 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Session India Pale Ale (IPA) is a style of pale ale. The colour of an IPA can vary from a light gold to a reddish amber." ;
              rdfs:label "SESSION_INDIA_PALE_ALE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169921" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169922
gdsn:cv169922 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Smoke porter is a dark style of beer from well-hopped beers made from brown malt." ;
              rdfs:label "SMOKE_PORTER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169922" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169923
gdsn:cv169923 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Bernsteinfarbenes Weizen is a style of Weizenbock. Weizenbock is a style of bock brewed using wheat instead of barley. The style combines darker Munich malts and top-fermenting wheat beer yeast, brewed at the strength of a doppelbock." ;
              rdfs:label "SOUTH_GERMAN_STYLE_BERNSTEINFARBENES_WEIZEN" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169923" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169924
gdsn:cv169924 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The German-style Dunkelweizen can be considered a cross between a German-style Dunkel and a hefeweizen. Distinguished by its sweet maltiness and chocolate-like character, it can also have banana and clove (and occasionally vanilla or bubblegum) esters from weizen ale yeast." ;
              rdfs:label "SOUTH_GERMAN_STYLE_DUNKEL_WEIZEN" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169924" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169925
gdsn:cv169925 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Hefeweizen is particularly noted for its low hop bitterness (about 15 IBUs) and relatively high carbonation (approaching four volumes), considered important to balance the beer's relatively malty sweetness. Another balancing flavour note unique to Hefeweizen beer is its phenolic character; its signature phenol is 4-vinyl guaiacol,[8] a metabolite of ferulic acid, the result of fermentation by top-fermenting yeast appropriate for the style." ;
              rdfs:label "SOUTH_GERMAN_STYLE_HEFEWEIZEN" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169925" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169926
gdsn:cv169926 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "This wheat beer, sometimes called “Kristal Weissbier,” is filtered after fermentation to remove yeast. The result is a crystal-clear weizen beer with no haze or clouds. Exhibiting aroma and flavour characteristics similar to Hefeweizen, Kristalweizen German beer is generally perceived as more crisp and clean on the palate." ;
              rdfs:label "SOUTH_GERMAN_STYLE_KRISTAL_WEIZEN" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169926" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv169927
gdsn:cv169927 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1041249980 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "South German Style Weizenbock is a style of bock. Crafted originally in Southern Germany brewed using wheat instead of barley. The style combines darker Munich malts and top fermenting wheat beer yeast, brewed at the strength of a Doppelbock." ;
              rdfs:label "SOUTH_GERMAN_STYLE_WEIZENBOCK" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "BeerStyleTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "169927" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


