###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170103
gdsn:cv170103 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c755936217 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A surrounding net is a fishing net which surrounds fish and other aquatic animals on the sides and underneath. Surrounding nets are divided into: • Purse seines • Surrounding nets without purse lines • Surrounding nets (not enough information)" ;
              rdfs:label "01" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "CatchMethodCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170103" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170104
gdsn:cv170104 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c755936217 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A seine net is a fishing net that hangs vertically in the water with its bottom edge held down by weights and its top edge buoyed by floats. Seine nets can be deployed from the shore as a beach seine, or from a boat. Seine nets are divided into: • Beach seines • Boat seines • Seine nets (not enough information)" ;
              rdfs:label "02" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "CatchMethodCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170104" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170105
gdsn:cv170105 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c755936217 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Trawls are cone-shaped net (made from two, four or more panels) which are towed, by one or two boats, on the bottom or in midwater (pelagic). Trawls are divided into: • Beam trawls • Single boat bottom otter trawls • Twin bottom otter trawls • Multiple bottom otter trawls • Bottom pair trawls • Bottom trawls • Single boat midwater otter trawls • Midwater pair trawls • Midwater trawls (not enough information) • Semi-pelagic trawls • Trawls (not enough information)" ;
              rdfs:label "03" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "CatchMethodCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170105" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170106
gdsn:cv170106 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c755936217 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Dredges are gears which are dragged along the bottom to catch shellfish. They consist of a mouth frame to which a holding bag constructed of metal rings or meshes is attached. Dredges are divided into: • Towed dredges • Hand dredges • Mechanized dredges • Dredges (not enough information)" ;
              rdfs:label "04" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "CatchMethodCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170106" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170107
gdsn:cv170107 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c755936217 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Lift nets are horizontal netting panels or bag shaped like a parallelepiped, pyramid or cone with the opening facing upwards which are submerged at a certain depth, left for a while, the time necessary for light or bait to attract fish over the opening, then lifted out of the water. Lift nets are divided into: • Portable lift nets • Boat-operated lift nets • Shore-operated stationary lift nets • Lift nets (not enough information)" ;
              rdfs:label "05" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "CatchMethodCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170107" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170108
gdsn:cv170108 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c755936217 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Gillnets and entangling nets are strings of single, double or triple netting walls, vertical, near by the surface, in midwater on on the bottom, in which fish will gill, entangle or enmesh. Gillnets and entangling nets have floats on the upper line (headrope) and, in general, weights on the ground-line (footrope). Gillnets and entangling nets are divided into: • Set gillnets (anchored) • Drift gillnets • Encircling gillnets • Gillnets and entangling nets (not enough information)" ;
              rdfs:label "07" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "CatchMethodCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170108" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170109
gdsn:cv170109 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c755936217 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Traps, large stationary nets or barrages or pots, are gears in which the fish are retained or enter voluntarily and will be hampered from escaping. They are designed in such manner that the entrance itself became a non-return device, allowing the fish to enter the trap but making it impossible to leave the catching chamber. Traps are divided into: • Stationary uncovered pound nets • Pots • Fyke nets • Stow nets • Barriers, fences, weirs, etc • Aerial traps • Traps (not enough information)" ;
              rdfs:label "08" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "CatchMethodCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170109" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170110
gdsn:cv170110 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c755936217 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Hooks and lines are gear where the fish is attracted by a natural or artificial bait (lures) placed on a hook fixed to the end of a line or snood, on which they get caught. Hooks or metallic points (jigs) are also used to catch fish by ripping them when they pass in its range of movement. Hooks and lines are divided into: • Handlines and hand-operated pole-and-lines • Mechanised lines and pole-and-lines • Set longlines • Drifting longlines • Longlines (not enough information) • Vertical lines • Trolling lines • Hooks and lines (not enough information)" ;
              rdfs:label "09" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "CatchMethodCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170110" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170111
gdsn:cv170111 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c755936217 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Boat dredges" ;
              rdfs:label "DRB" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "CatchMethodCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170111" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


