###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170444
gdsn:cv170444 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-2060056022 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A strip of material which is coated with adhesives or glues which can be" ;
              rdfs:label "ADHESIVE_STRIPS" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "ClosureOrFastenerTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170444" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170445
gdsn:cv170445 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-2060056022 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A pin buckle or clasp is a device used for fastening two loose ends, with one attached to it and the other held with a pin (also named prong) in a secure but adjustable manner, e.g. for watches or belts." ;
              rdfs:label "BUCKLES_OR_CLASPS" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "ClosureOrFastenerTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170445" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170446
gdsn:cv170446 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-2060056022 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A button is usually a disk-like piece of solid material having holes or a shank through which it is sewed to one side of an article of clothing and used to fasten or close the garment by passing through a loop or hole in the other side." ;
              rdfs:label "BUTTONS" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "ClosureOrFastenerTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170446" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170447
gdsn:cv170447 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-2060056022 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A cable tie or tie-wrap, also known as a hose tie, zap-strap, or zip tie,[1] is a type of fastener, for holding items together, primarily electric cables or wires." ;
              rdfs:label "CABLE_TIE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "ClosureOrFastenerTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170447" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170448
gdsn:cv170448 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-2060056022 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A bulldog clip is a device for temporarily binding sheets of paper together. It consists of a rectangular sheet of springy steel curved into a cylinder, with two flat steel strips inserted to form combined handles and jaws. The user presses the two handles together, causing the jaws to open against the force of the spring, then inserts a stack of papers and releases the handles. The spring forces the jaws together, gripping the papers firmly." ;
              rdfs:label "CLIP_BULLDOG" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "ClosureOrFastenerTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170448" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170449
gdsn:cv170449 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-2060056022 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A paper clip (or sometimes paperclip) is an instrument used to hold sheets of paper together, usually made of steel wire bent to a looped shape." ;
              rdfs:label "CLIP_PAPER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "ClosureOrFastenerTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170449" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170450
gdsn:cv170450 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-2060056022 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The folding clasp is a type of closure for watch straps. It is most commonly found in metal bandes. In contrast to the pin buckle, the bracelet is not fully opened with the folding clasp but is opened (folded up) on hinges. This widens the bracelet and it can be removed from the arm." ;
              rdfs:label "FOLDING_CLASP" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "ClosureOrFastenerTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170450" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170451
gdsn:cv170451 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-2060056022 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Round grommets look like metal or plastic rings that help reinforce holes. A cord or lace threads through the hole, also known as the eye. A grommet press or a grommet setting tool and a small hammer help fasten the grommet to the garment. (See Reference 3) Examples of grommets are found on laced running shoes and laced clothing. A grommet belt allows a person to adjust the fit by inserting a buckle's metal pin through a reinforced hole." ;
              rdfs:label "GROMMETS" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "ClosureOrFastenerTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170451" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170452
gdsn:cv170452 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-2060056022 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Hooks and eyes consist of two parts that interlock. The hook part features a curved shape. The eye has an opening which resembles a U-shape into which the hook is inserted to clsoe the item." ;
              rdfs:label "HOOK_AND_EYES" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "ClosureOrFastenerTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170452" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170453
gdsn:cv170453 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-2060056022 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "This variety of fastener is closed by pressure and opened by pulling it apart. These fasteners are made of tiny, firm, hooks on one part and softer loops on the other. The size of the fastener indicates its holding strength." ;
              rdfs:label "HOOK_AND_LOOP_FASTENERS" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "ClosureOrFastenerTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170453" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170454
gdsn:cv170454 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-2060056022 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A Jeans Button is generally used as a method of fastening for denim trousers or denim jackets." ;
              rdfs:label "JEANS_BUTTON" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "ClosureOrFastenerTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170454" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170455
gdsn:cv170455 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-2060056022 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Shoelaces, sometimes called shoestrings (US English) or bootlaces (UK English), are a system commonly used to secure shoes, boots and other footwear. Laces can also be used for other types of items, but function similarly to shoelaces. Laces typically consist of a strings or cords, finished off at both ends with stiff sections, commonly known as aglets. The lace typically passes through a series of holes, eyelets, loops or hooks on either side of the closure. Loosening or removing the lacing allows the item to open, while tightening the lacing and tying off the ends secures the item." ;
              rdfs:label "LACES_OR_SHOELACES" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "ClosureOrFastenerTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170455" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv170456
gdsn:cv170456 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-2060056022 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The value needed is not listed or is not defined within this list’s individual code values and definitions. Please send a work request into GS1 or your solution provider requesting the code you are searching for." ;
              rdfs:label "OTHER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "ClosureOrFastenerTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "170456" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


