              rdfs:comment "Bushel (UK): A bushel is an imperial and U.S. customary unit of dry volume, equivalent in each of these systems to 4 pecks or 8 gallons. It is used for volumes of dry commodities (not liquids), most often in agriculture" ;
              rdfs:label "BUI" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "FunctionalBasisUnitCode" ;
