              rdfs:comment "The tricorne is a three-sided hat whose brim is folded up against a rounded crown. Sometimes referred to as a \"pirate hat,\" the tricorne has a modern association with pirate costuming, as well as an historical association with maritime and 18th and 19th-century military uniforms. Two-sided (or \"bicorne,\" a shape associated with the Napoleonic era) novelty hats bearing the skull-and-crossbones may be included here." ;
