              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A unit used for quantifying the vitamin A value of sources of vitamin A, including both preformed retinoids and precursor carotenoids. Examples include: . One RE is equivalent to 1 mcg of retinol, 6 mcg of Beta-carotene, or 12 mcg of other pro-vitamin A carotenoids. . One RE is equivalent to 0.3 International Units of retinol or 0.1 International Units of Beta-carotene." ;
              rdfs:label "XRE" ;
