              rdfs:comment "To indicate the bicobial count of aerobe mesophiles determined according to local target market regulations. Aerobe: an organism that grows in the presence of oxygen. There may be facultative or obligate aerobes. Mesophile: organism living in the temperature range around that of warm-blooded animals, usually between 20-45°C." ;
              rdfs:label "AEROBE_MESOPHILES_MICROBIAL_COUNT" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "MicrobiologicalOrganismCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "172941" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


