###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv173063
gdsn:cv173063 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-519231 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Halogenated organic flame retardants are intended to inhibit ignition and the spread of flames. Halogenated chemicals are chemicals that contain bromine, chlorine, fluorine or iodine bonded to a carbon atom." ;
              rdfs:label "BFR_HFR" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "NonfoodIngredientOfConcernCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "173063" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv173064
gdsn:cv173064 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-519231 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Bisphenol is an organic compound with the chemical formula (CH3)2C(C6H4OH)2. It is a colourless solid that is soluble in organic solvents, but poorly soluble in water. BPA is controversial because it exerts weak, but detectable, hormone-like properties, raising concerns about its presence in consumer products and foods contained in such products" ;
              rdfs:label "BPA" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "NonfoodIngredientOfConcernCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "173064" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv173065
gdsn:cv173065 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-519231 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Di-(2-ethylhexyl) phthalate (DEHP) is a member of the phthalate family used as a softening agent for many PVC applications. DEHP is sometimes called dioctyl phthalate (DOP) or Bis(2-ethylhexyl)phthalate (BEHP). In the EU package markings require a mark to show \"PHT\"." ;
              rdfs:label "DEHP" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "NonfoodIngredientOfConcernCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "173065" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv173066
gdsn:cv173066 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-519231 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Mercury is a naturally occurring element that is found in air, water and soil. It exists in several forms: elemental or metallic mercury, inorganic mercury compounds, and organic mercury compounds." ;
              rdfs:label "HG" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "NonfoodIngredientOfConcernCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "173066" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv173067
gdsn:cv173067 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-519231 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "If any portion of this item, including reusable packaging, is made from wood or paper, then answer “Yes”. Reusable packaging is intended to stay in use with the product. Ex: Wooden box in which a lawn game, such as a croquet set, is stored after use." ;
              rdfs:label "PAPER_WOOD" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "NonfoodIngredientOfConcernCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "173067" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


