###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv173869
gdsn:cv173869 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1438 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "GS1 Tagname Description: Bacillus coagulans is approved for veterinary purposes as GRAS by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration's Center for Veterinary Medicine, as well as by the European Union, and is listed by AAFCO for use as a direct-fed microbial in livestock production. It is often used in veterinary applications, especially as a probiotic in pigs, cattle, poultry, and shrimp. Many references to use of this bacterium in humans exist, especially in improving the vaginal flora, improving abdominal pain and bloating in irritable bowel syndrome patients, and increasing immune response to viral challenges. There is evidence from animal research that suggests that Bacillus coagulans is effective in both treating as well as preventing recurrence of clostridium difficile associated diarrhea. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bacillus_coagulans - UOM for Nutrient Panel: - GS1 Notes, Keywords, and Examples: - GS1 Comment: GS1 temporary code - GS1 Synonyms:" ;
              rdfs:label "X_BACCOA" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "NutrientTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "http://www.fao.org/infoods/infoods/standards-guidelines/food-component-identifiers-tagnames/en/" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "173869" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv173870
gdsn:cv173870 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1438 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "GS1 Tagname Description: Bacillus subtilis is a gram-positive, catalase-positive bacterium, found in soil and the gastrointestinal tract of ruminants, humans and marine sponges. It is an immunostimulatory agent to aid treatment of gastrointestinal and urinary tract diseases. - UOM for Nutrient Panel: MGM or CFU - GS1 Notes, Keywords, and Examples: - GS1 Comment: GS1 temporary code - GS1 Synonyms: Hay bacillus, Grass bacillus, CAS: 68038-70-0" ;
              rdfs:label "X_BACILLUS_SUBTILIS" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "NutrientTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "http://www.fao.org/infoods/infoods/standards-guidelines/food-component-identifiers-tagnames/en/" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "173870" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


