              rdfs:comment "Fully hydrogenated vegetable oils are solid fats, produced from liquid, typically vegetable, oils by full hydrogenation. Full hydrogenation results in fats very high in saturated fatty acids (SAFA). Fully hydrogenated vegetable oils do not contain significant amounts of artificial trans fatty acids (TFA)." ;
