                       gdsn:c2147348062 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A milky fluid found in many plants, such as poppies and spurges, which exudes when the plant is cut and coagulates on exposure to the air. The latex of the rubber tree is the chief source of natural rubber. Also, a synthetic product resembling latex, consisting of a dispersion in water of polymer particles, used to make paints, coatings, and other products." ;
