###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv176746
gdsn:cv176746 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The logo stands for regional and domestic products which are produced, processed and prepared in a given geographical area using recognised quality standards. Only local products with 100 percent guarantee of origin are given this seal. It is given not only the green Ländle brand products but also other products that keep clearly defined in writing and retained quality guidelines." ;
              rdfs:label "LAENDLE_QUALITAET" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "http://www.laendle.at/" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "176746" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv176747
gdsn:cv176747 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "In 2015, a new logo began to appear on French milk cartons and bottles: \"Milk collected and packaged in France\". This logo was created on the initiative of French professionals in the liquid milk sector, brought together within Syndilait, and is supported by the Ministry of Agriculture and the FNPL (National Federation of Milk Producers). Two years after its launch, this logo is a great success with professionals in the sector, distributors and consumers, as it is already present on more than 60% of the bottles and cartons of milk on sale." ;
              rdfs:label "LAIT_COLLECTE_ET_CONDITIONNE_EN_FRANCE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "http://leblogdulait.fr/actualites/logo-lait-collecte-conditionne-france-fort-de-succes-logo-se-decline-dautres-produits-laitiers-/" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "176747" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv176748
gdsn:cv176748 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A new complementary logo for dairy products other than drinking milk. Professionals in the sector have decided to go further in this citizen, collective and responsible approach in favour of French milk by using the logo \"Milk collected and processed in France\" on other products resulting from the processing of milk such as milk drinks, cream, cheese, fresh products or butter. All of these products are now able to carry a the logo \"Milk collected and processed in France\" while the logo \"Milk collected and packaged in France\" remains reserved for drinking milk." ;
              rdfs:label "LAIT_COLLECTE_ET_TRANSFORME_EN_FRANCE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "http://leblogdulait.fr/actualites/logo-lait-collecte-conditionne-france-fort-de-succes-logo-se-decline-dautres-produits-laitiers-/" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "176748" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv176749
gdsn:cv176749 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The French agricultural organizations have created a common visual identity in order to highlight the French origin of agricultural products in this case rabbit: the signatures \"Agricultural Products of France\". Remarkable to their elegant silhouette in a tricolor pentagon that is available for each family of products, these signatures reflect the commitment of the professionals of the sectors to value the know-how, the territories and the French jobs. Covering a variety of productions, these signatures all have a common basis, which consists of four criteria: Origin France of the products concerned, The existence of specifications or regulations governing the use of the logo, A formal commitment from the operators of the sectors concerned wishing to use these logos, Controls performed by a third party." ;
              rdfs:label "LAPIN_DE_FRANCE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "http://www.produitsagricolesdefrance.fr" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "176749" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv176750
gdsn:cv176750 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The French agricultural organizations have created a common visual identity in order to highlight the French origin of agricultural products in this case pork: the signatures \"Agricultural Products of France\". Remarkable to their elegant silhouette in a tricolor pentagon that is available for each family of products, these signatures reflect the commitment of the professionals of the sectors to value the know-how, the territories and the French jobs. Covering a variety of productions, these signatures all have a common basis, which consists of four criteria: Origin France of the products concerned, The existence of specifications or regulations governing the use of the logo, A formal commitment from the operators of the sectors concerned wishing to use these logos, Controls performed by a third party." ;
              rdfs:label "LE_PORC_FRANCAIS" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "http://www.produitsagricolesdefrance.fr" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "176750" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv176751
gdsn:cv176751 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The Coalition for Consumer Information on Cosmetics (CCIC) Leaping Bunny Program administers a cruelty-free standard and the internationally recognized Leaping Bunny Logo for companies producing cosmetic, personal care, and household products. The Leaping Bunny Program provides the best assurance that no new animal testing is used in any phase of product development by the company, its laboratories, or suppliers. See also www.leapingbunny.org" ;
              rdfs:label "LEAPING_BUNNY" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "www.leapingbunny.org" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "176751" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv176752
gdsn:cv176752 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Vegetable producers created the National Federation of Vegetable Producers in 1946. Vegetables (FNPL) to defend and promote their profession. It federates producers of vegetables and represents all vegetable production intended to be used in the production of marketed fresh. It became the Producteurs de Légumes de France in 2008. The Producteurs de Légumes de France work to defend the interests of the producers of and improving the profitability and competitiveness of their businesses by intervening on all subjects that concern them." ;
              rdfs:label "LEGUMES_DE_FRANCE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "http://www.legumesdefrance.fr/sites/fnplegweb/livre_blanc_2017.pdf http://www.legumesdefrance.fr/sites/fnplegweb/" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "176752" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv176753
gdsn:cv176753 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Certification is a process in which an independent third party certification body, as LETIS, ensures compliance with a specific standard. At LETIS, compliance is assessed by a methodical system of audits, accredited by national and international monitoring and accreditation bodies" ;
              rdfs:label "LETIS_ORGANIC" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "http://www.letis.org/?lang=en" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "176753" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv176754
gdsn:cv176754 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "According to the LGA (Landesgewerbeanstalt Bayern) directive, checks are done on security, features, usability, performance, electromagnetic compatibility (EMC) and hygiene of various products. The LGA has become part of TÜV, this quality mark is therefore issued by TÜV." ;
              rdfs:label "LGA" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "www.tuv.com / www.lga.de" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "176754" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv176755
gdsn:cv176755 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Localize is the only Local shelf label program in North America. We are dedicated to continuously collecting, growing, and ensuring the integrity of our data. Localize’s powerful database and application contain geographical and socially relevant information that is valuable for grocers and vital to shoppers looking for information at the shelf-edge" ;
              rdfs:label "LOCALIZE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "http://www.localizeyourfood.com/" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "176755" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


