              rdfs:comment "Hip hop music, also known as rap music, is a style of music which came into existence in the United States during the mid-1970s, and became a large part of modern pop culture during the 1980s. It consists of two main components: rapping (MCing) and DJing (production and scratching)." ;
              rdfs:label "HIP_HOP_RAP" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "ProductGenreTypeCode (Music)" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "178350" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


