###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180634
gdsn:cv180634 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348280 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A non-specific polymer of a vinyl compound or a product (as a resin or a textile fibre) made from such a polymer." ;
              rdfs:label "VINYL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "MaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180634" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180635
gdsn:cv180635 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348280 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Fibre formed of linear macromolecules whose chain is constituted by poly(vinyl alcohol) with differing levels of acetalisation." ;
              rdfs:label "FIBRE_VINYLAL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "MaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180635" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180636
gdsn:cv180636 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348280 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Regenerated cellulose fibre obtained by the viscose process for filament and discontinuous fibre." ;
              rdfs:label "FIBRE_VISCOSE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "MaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180636" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180637
gdsn:cv180637 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348280 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Hardboard (not to be confused with hardwood), also called High-Density Fiberboard (HDF), is a type of fibreboard, which is similar to particle board and medium-density fiberboard, but is denser, much stronger and harder because it is made out of exploded wood fibres which have been highly compressed. Consequently, the density of hardboard is 31 lbs or more per cubic foot (500 kg/m³)[2] and is usually about 50-65 lbs per cubic foot (800–1040 kg/m³). It differs from particle board in that the bonding of the wood fibers requires no additional materials, although resin is often added. Unlike particle board, it will not split or crack." ;
              rdfs:label "WOOD_HARDBOARD" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "MaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180637" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180638
gdsn:cv180638 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348280 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A general term referring to any variety of broad-leaved, deciduous trees, and the wood from those trees. The term has nothing to do with the actual hardness of the wood; some hardwoods are softer than certain softwood (evergreen) species." ;
              rdfs:label "WOOD_HARDWOOD" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "MaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180638" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180639
gdsn:cv180639 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348280 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Medium-Density Fibreboard (MDF) is an engineered wood product made by breaking down hardwood or softwood residuals into wood fibres, combining them with wax and a resin binder, and forming panels by applying high temperature and pressure. MDF is generally denser than plywood. It is made up of separated fibres, but can be used as a building material similar in application to plywood. It is stronger and much more dense than particle board." ;
              rdfs:label "WOOD_MEDIUM_DENSITY_FIBREBOARD" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "MaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180639" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180640
gdsn:cv180640 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348280 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Oriented Strand Board (OSB), also known as sterling board, sterling OSB, aspenite, and smartply, is an engineered wood particle board formed by adding adhesives and then compressing layers of wood strands (flakes) in specific orientations. OSB may have a rough and variegated surface with the individual strips of around 2.5 × 15 cm (1\" × 6\"), lying unevenly across each other and comes in a variety of types." ;
              rdfs:label "WOOD_ORIENTED_STRANDBOARD" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "MaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180640" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180641
gdsn:cv180641 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348280 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The value needed is not listed or is not defined within this list’s individual code value and definitions of wood. Please send a work request into GS1 or your solution provider requesting the code you are searching for." ;
              rdfs:label "WOOD_OTHER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "MaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180641" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180642
gdsn:cv180642 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348280 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Particle Board, also known as particleboard, chipboard, and Low-Density Fibreboard (LDF), is an engineered wood product manufactured from wood chips, sawmill shavings, or sawdust, and a synthetic resin or other suitable binder, which is pressed and extruded. Particle board is a composite material." ;
              rdfs:label "WOOD_PARTICLE_BOARD" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "MaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180642" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180643
gdsn:cv180643 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348280 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Plywood, a manufactured wood panel similar to LDF, MDF, and HDF, is made from layering thin sheets of wood. Plywood layers (called veneers or plies) are glued together, with adjacent plies having their wood grain rotated relative to adjacent layers up to 90 degrees. All plywoods bind resin and wood fibre sheets (cellulose cells are long, strong and thin) to form a composite material." ;
              rdfs:label "WOOD_PLYWOOD" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "MaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180643" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180644
gdsn:cv180644 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348280 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "General term used to describe lumber produced from needle and/or cone bearing trees (Conifers)." ;
              rdfs:label "WOOD_SOFTWOOD" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "MaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180644" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180645
gdsn:cv180645 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348280 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Fibre from sheep's or lambs’ fleeces (Ovis aries) or a mixture of fibres from sheep's or lambs’ fleeces and the hair of the following animals: alpaca, llama, camel, kashmir goat, angora goat, angora rabbit, vicuna, yak, guanaco, cashgora goat, beaver, otter." ;
              rdfs:label "FIBRE_WOOL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "MaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180645" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180646
gdsn:cv180646 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1438 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "GS1 Tagname Description: Resin made from Boswellia extract (bot.: Boswellia serrata) - UOM for Nutrient Panel: mg - GS1 Notes, Keywords, and Examples: - GS1 Comment: GS1 temporary code - GS1 Synonyms: - Indian incense, Indian frankincense, CAS number: 97952-72-2" ;
              rdfs:label "X_BOSWELLIA_RESIN_EXTRACT" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "NutrientTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180646" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180647
gdsn:cv180647 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1438 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "GS1 Tagname Description: Gamma-Aminobutyric acid, or GABA, is the chief inhibitory neurotransmitter in the developmentally mature mammalian central nervous system. Its principal role is reducing neuronal excitability throughout the nervous system. GABA is known for producing a calming effect for controlling anxiety, stress and fear. - UOM for Nutrient Panel: MGM - GS1 Notes, Keywords, and Examples: - GS1 Comment: GS1 temporary code - GS1 Synonyms: GABA, γ-Aminobutyric acid, Piperidic acid, Piperidinic acid, CAS number: 56-12-2" ;
              rdfs:label "X_G_AMINOBUTYRIC_ACID" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "NutrientTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180647" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180648
gdsn:cv180648 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1438 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "GS1 Tagname Description: Golden poppy extract (bot.: Eschscholzia californica) - UOM for Nutrient Panel: mg - GS1 Notes, Keywords, and Examples: - GS1 Comment: GS1 temporary code - GS1 Synonyms: California poppy, California sunlight or cup of gold" ;
              rdfs:label "X_GOLDEN_POPPY_EXTRACT" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "NutrientTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180648" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180649
gdsn:cv180649 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1438 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "GS1 Tagname Description: L-Theanine is an amino acid analogue of the proteinogenic amino acids. Theanine provides a unique brothy or savoury (umami) flavour to green tea infusions. - UOM for Nutrient Panel: MGM - GS1 Notes, Keywords, and Examples: - GS1 Comment: GS1 temporary code - GS1 Synonyms: Theanine, CAS number: 3081-61-6" ;
              rdfs:label "X_L_THEANINE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "NutrientTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180649" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180650
gdsn:cv180650 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1438 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "GS1 Tagname Description: Manuka honey (MGO) is made in Australia and New Zealand by bees that pollinate the native leptospermum scoparium bush (also known as a tea tree). Advocates say it can treat wound infections and other conditions.- UOM for Nutrient Panel: MGM - GS1 Notes, Keywords, and Examples: - GS1 Comment: GS1 temporary code - GS1 Synonyms: MGO, CAS: 91052-92-5" ;
              rdfs:label "X_MANUKA_HONEY" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "NutrientTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180650" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180651
gdsn:cv180651 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1438 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "GS1 Tagname Description: Withania somnifera or ashwagandha, is an evergreen shrub in the Solanaceae or nightshade family. It is most common used as a dietary supplement. - UOM for Nutrient Panel: MGM - GS1 Notes, Keywords, and Examples: - GS1 Comment: GS1 temporary code - GS1 Synonyms: Ashwagandha, Winter Cherry, Indian Ginseng, CAS number: 90147-43-6" ;
              rdfs:label "X_WITHANIA_SOMNIFERA" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "NutrientTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180651" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180652
gdsn:cv180652 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The label confirms, the audit and certification of a product’s carbon footprint by the accreditation body Société Générale de Surveillance (SGS) based on the reference of ISO standard 14067 for the carbon footprint of products (CFP)." ;
              rdfs:label "CARBON_NEUTRAL_SGS" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "www.sgs.com" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180652" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180653
gdsn:cv180653 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The Bundesverband der Industrie- und Handelsunternehmen (BDIH) COSMOS logo with signature “natural” is used to certify products which comply with the COSMOS-standard and are containing less than 20% of organic origin." ;
              rdfs:label "COSMOS_NATURAL_BDIH" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "https://www.kontrollierte-naturkosmetik.de/index.htm" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180653" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180654
gdsn:cv180654 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The Bundesverband der Industrie- und Handelsunternehmen (BDIH) COSMOS logo with signature „organic“ is used to certify products which comply with the COSMOS-standard and contain the required percentages of organic ingredients (> 20%) as specified in the COSMOS standard." ;
              rdfs:label "COSMOS_ORGANIC_BDIH" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "https://www.kontrollierte-naturkosmetik.de/index.htm" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180654" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180655
gdsn:cv180655 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The \"Biodynamisch\" on the Demeter guaranteed label, indicates that products contain at least 95 percent organic and 90 percent Demeter ingredients. The label is issued by the association Demeter e.V." ;
              rdfs:label "DEMETER_GUARANTEED" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "https://www.demeter.de/lebensmittel-produkte/einkaufen" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180655" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180656
gdsn:cv180656 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The ECOCERT logo with signature “NATURAL DETERGENT” is used to certify detergents which comply with the ECOCERT Standard. Also labeled as \"Ecocert Ecodetergent\"" ;
              rdfs:label "ECOCERT_NATURAL_DETERGENT" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "packagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "https://www.ecocert.com" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180656" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180657
gdsn:cv180657 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c-1409540287 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The ECOCERT logo with signature “NATURAL DETERGENT made with ORGANIC” is used to certify detergents which comply with the ECOCERT Standard made from at least 10% organic raw materials." ;
              rdfs:label "ECOCERT_NATURAL_DETERGENT_MADE_WITH_ORGANIC" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMarkedLabelAccreditationCode" ;
              gdsn:externalLink "https://www.ecocert.com" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180657" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180658
