###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180891
gdsn:cv180891 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348240 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Renewable material and renewable feedstock (raw material used in industrial process or as fuel) with virgin raw materials in the production process. This creates a final product that is a mixture of virgin and renewable content. Mass balance is about mixing fossil and renewable/recycled materials. It's important to note that individual packaging may not necessarily include renewable material, but the plastic material producer is certified for mass balance and incorporates a specific percentage of renewable materials in their feedstock. Refer to local regulations." ;
              rdfs:label "RENEWABLE_MATERIAL_MASS_BALANCE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingClaimElementCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180891" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180892
gdsn:cv180892 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348240 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Recycled material and feedstock are combined with virgin raw materials in the production process, resulting in a final product that contains both virgin and recycled content. Mass balance involves mixing fossil and recycled/renewable materials to meet this objective. It's important to note that individual packaging may not necessarily include recycled material, but the plastic material producer is certified for mass balance and incorporates a specific percentage of recycled materials in their feedstock. Refer to local regulations." ;
              rdfs:label "RECYCLED_MATERIAL_MASS_BALANCE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingClaimElementCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180892" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180893
gdsn:cv180893 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348241 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A claim that the packaging is manufactured with/from a specific feature, and any claim likely to have the same meaning for the consumer. Please refer to any local regulations that determine containment levels for the claim." ;
              rdfs:label "MADE_WITH" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingClaimTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180893" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180894
gdsn:cv180894 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348241 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A claim that the packaging is 100% manufactured with/from a specific feature, and any claim likely to have the same meaning for the consumer. Please refer to any local regulations that determine containment levels for the claim." ;
              rdfs:label "MADE_WITH_100_PERCENT" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingClaimTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180894" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180895
gdsn:cv180895 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348241 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A claim that the packaging is partially manufactured with/from a specific feature, and any claim likely to have the same meaning for the consumer. Please refer to any local regulations that determine containment levels for the claim." ;
              rdfs:label "PARTIALLY_MADE_WITH" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingClaimTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180895" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180896
gdsn:cv180896 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348240 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Biodegradable refers to the ability of things to get disintegrated (decomposed) by the action of micro-organisms such as bacteria or fungi biological (with or without oxygen) while getting assimilated into the natural environment." ;
              rdfs:label "BIODEGRADABLE_MATERIAL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingClaimElementCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180896" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180897
gdsn:cv180897 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348240 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Wind power or wind energy is mostly the use of wind turbines to generate electricity. Wind power is a popular, sustainable, renewable energy source that has a much smaller impact on the environment than burning fossil fuels." ;
              rdfs:label "WIND_POWER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingClaimElementCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180897" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180898
gdsn:cv180898 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348240 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Biogas is a naturally occurring and renewable source of energy, resulting from the breakdown of organic matter." ;
              rdfs:label "BIOGAS" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingClaimElementCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180898" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180899
gdsn:cv180899 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348240 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A recycled material refers to any substance that has undergone a process of reprocessing or reclamation to be used again in the manufacturing of new products. Recycled materials can encompass a wide range of items, including paper, glass, metal, plastics, textiles, and more." ;
              rdfs:label "RECYCLED_MATERIAL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingClaimElementCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180899" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180900
gdsn:cv180900 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348240 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A renewable material is a material made of natural resources that can be replenished." ;
              rdfs:label "RENEWABLE_MATERIAL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingClaimElementCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180900" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180901
gdsn:cv180901 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348242 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "An adhesive that is made with components that are all not water soluble (i.e., will not dissolve in water)." ;
              rdfs:label "NON_WATER_SOLUBLE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMaterialAdhesiveSolubilityTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180901" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180902
gdsn:cv180902 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348242 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "An adhesive which is alkaline soluble or releasable." ;
              rdfs:label "ALKALINE_SOLUBLE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMaterialAdhesiveSolubilityTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180902" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180903
gdsn:cv180903 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348242 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "An adhesive which is water soluble or water releasable." ;
              rdfs:label "WATER_SOLUBLE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMaterialAdhesiveSolubilityTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180903" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180904
gdsn:cv180904 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348243 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The value needed is not listed or is not defined within this list’s individual code values and definitions. Please send a work request into GS1 or your solution provider requesting the code you are searching for." ;
              rdfs:label "OTHER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMaterialAdhesiveTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180904" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180905
gdsn:cv180905 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348243 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A solid formulation based on thermoplastic polymers, no water or solvents are involved. Also known as hot glue." ;
              rdfs:label "HOT_MELT" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMaterialAdhesiveTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180905" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180906
gdsn:cv180906 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348243 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A versatile water resistant polymer whose primary ingredient is silica, a common form of sand found in quartz." ;
              rdfs:label "SILICONE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "PackagingMaterialAdhesiveTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180906" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180907
gdsn:cv180907 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348256 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The material is made from bio-based polymers whole or partially from renewable biological resources, like sugar cane, starch." ;
              rdfs:label "BIOLOGICAL_PLASTIC" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "RawMaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180907" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180908
gdsn:cv180908 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348256 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The material is made from crude oil." ;
              rdfs:label "CRUDE_OIL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "RawMaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180908" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180909
gdsn:cv180909 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348256 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The material is made from virgin, non-recycled raw materials, such as aluminium or wood." ;
              rdfs:label "NEW_RAW_MATERIAL_OTHER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "RawMaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180909" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180910
gdsn:cv180910 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348256 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The material is made from post consumer recycled content." ;
              rdfs:label "RECYCLED" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "RawMaterialCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180910" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180911
gdsn:cv180911 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Geraniol is a monoterpenoid which is a primary component of citronella oil, rose oil, palmarosa oil and lemongrass. It has a rose and fruity aroma. Example: it is found in low amounts in cannabis strains. CAS number: 106-24-1" ;
              rdfs:label "GERANIOL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180911" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180912
gdsn:cv180912 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Myrcene is a monoterpene which occurs widely in essential oils. It exudes a musky herbal aroma. Example: Myrcene is found in large concentrations in the cannabis plant. Also known as beta-myrcene or β-myrcene. CAS number: 123-35-3" ;
              rdfs:label "MYRCENE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180912" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180913
gdsn:cv180913 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Beta-caryophyllene is a constituent of many essential oils, especially clove oil, the oil from the stems and flowers of cloves, the essential oil of Cannabis sativa, rosemary and hops. Beta-caryophyllene is one of the chemical compounds that contributes to the aroma of black pepper. Example: It is the only terpene that acts as a cannabinoid. Also known as -β-caryophyllene or Caryophyllene. CAS number: 87-44-5" ;
              rdfs:label "BETA_CARYOPHYLLENE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180913" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180914
gdsn:cv180914 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Borneol is most commonly found in camphor but can also be found in a multitude of plants around the word such in ginger, rosemary, sage, cinnamon, mint and thyme. It has a cool, minty, and spicy scent. Example: it can be found in higher concentrations in certain strains of cannabis. CAS number: 507-70-0" ;
              rdfs:label "BORNEOL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180914" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180915
gdsn:cv180915 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Camphene is one of the most pervasive monoterpenes. It is found in low concentrations in many essential oils such as cypress, nutmeg, rosemary, camphor, neroli, ginger, and valerian. It has a strong earthy, woody and musky note. Example: it is a minor terpenes found in cannabis. CAS number: 79-92-5" ;
              rdfs:label "CAMPHENE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180915" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180916
gdsn:cv180916 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Cedrene is a sesquiterpene found in the essential oil of cedar. It has a fresh, woody and sweet scent. Example: it is a secondary terpene found in low levels in cannabis and cedar wood. It is also known as -α-cedrene. CAS number: 469-61-4" ;
              rdfs:label "CEDRENE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180916" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180917
gdsn:cv180917 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Humulene is a naturally sesquiterpene which is found in the essential oils of Humulus lupulus (hops) and other plants such as sage, ginger and ginseng. Its aroma is described as earthy, woody, with spicy, herbal notes. Example: Humulene typically appearing in lesser abundance in cannabis than other dominant terpenes. Also known as α-humulene or α-caryophyllene. CAS number: 6753-98-6" ;
              rdfs:label "HUMULENE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180917" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180918
gdsn:cv180918 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Isopulegol, an aromatic compound naturally found in herbs such as mint, geranium, and lemongrass. It acts as the natural precursor for menthol and is renowned for its minty and fresh scent. Example: Isopulegol is one of the secondary terpenes in cannabis. CAS number: 104870-56-6" ;
              rdfs:label "ISOPULEGOL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180918" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180919
gdsn:cv180919 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Menthol is a monoterpenoid which naturally occurs in plants such as peppermint and spearmint. It smells and tastes like mint and it is known for its cooling sensation. Example: Menthol is naturally occurs in trace amounts in cannabis. CAS number: 2216-51-5" ;
              rdfs:label "MENTHOL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180919" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180920
gdsn:cv180920 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Ocimene is a monoterpene found within a variety of plants and fruits including mint, parsley, mangoes, bergamot, kumquats and orchids. It has a sweet, citrusy and earthy aroma. Example: Ocimene is a common terpene found in some types of cannabis. CAS number: 502-99-8" ;
              rdfs:label "OCIMENE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180920" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180921
gdsn:cv180921 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Phellandrene is a terpene compound which is found in high amounts in eucalyptus plants. It has been also detected in lavender, ginger grass, pine, herbs and spices such as parsley, cinnamon, black pepper, and mint. It has a minty, citrus and woody smell. Example: Phellandrene is one of the secondary terpenes in cannabis. CAS number: 99-83-2" ;
              rdfs:label "PHELLANDRENE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180921" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180922
gdsn:cv180922 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The value needed is not listed or is not defined within this list’s individual code values and definitions. Please send a work request into GS1 or your solution provider requesting the code you are searching for." ;
              rdfs:label "OTHER" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180922" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180923
gdsn:cv180923 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Alpha-pinene is a monoterpene from a wide variety of plants including pine trees, Spanish sage, eucalyptus oils and oils of aromatic plants such as rosemary. It has a characteristic piney aroma. It is known to possess antimicrobial, apoptotic, antimetastatic, and antibiotic properties. Example: a common terpene found in cannabis. Also known as α-Pinene. CAS number: 80-56-8" ;
              rdfs:label "ALPHA_PINENE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180923" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180924
gdsn:cv180924 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Camphor is a waxy, colourless solid with a strong aroma. It is found in certain trees in the laurel family, the camphor tree in Southeast Asia, rosemary leaves, camphorweed, and camphor basil. Camphor is predominantly used for its scent, however, it is also said to have powerful anesthetic and antimicrobial properties. Example: Camphor produces an intense aroma responsible for the minty flavour in cannabis. CAS number: 76-22-2" ;
              rdfs:label "CAMPHOR" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180924" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180925
gdsn:cv180925 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Linalool is a monoterpenoid which is found in many flowers and spice plants. It has a strong floral and woody aroma. Example: Linalool is the most common terpene found in lavender and cannabis. CAS number: 78-70-6" ;
              rdfs:label "LINALOOL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180925" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180926
gdsn:cv180926 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Nerolidol is a naturally occurring sesquiterpene alcohol. It is found in the essential oils of many types of plants and flowers including ginger, lavender and tea tree. It has a woody and floral scent. Example: Nerolidol is found in some cannabis strains. Also known as peruviol and penetrol. CAS number: 7212-44-4" ;
              rdfs:label "NEROLIDOL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180926" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180927
gdsn:cv180927 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Bisabolol is a viscous oil that is found in plants like German Chamomile or certain types of shrubs. It a slightly woody, floral and a bit on the earthy side aroma. Example: high concentrations of bisabolo can be found in certain medicinal cannabis cultivars. Also known as α-bisabolol and levomenol. CAS number: 23089-26-1" ;
              rdfs:label "BISABOLOL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180927" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180928
gdsn:cv180928 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Carene is a monoterpene which is colourless liquid and has sweet and pungent odour. It can be found in plants such as basil, rosemary, cannabis and trees such as pines and cedars. It has a cedar, piney and citrusy aroma. Example: Carene can be inhaled when smoking or vaping cannabis strains with high amounts of it. Also known as 3-Carene. CAS number: 13466-78-9" ;
              rdfs:label "CARENE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180928" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180929
gdsn:cv180929 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Cymene is a monoterpene commonly found in hundreds of different plants including cumin, oregano, thyme, anise and coriander. It has a hint of citrus, earthy and woody aroma. Example: not a primary compound in cannabis and only shows up in small amounts in some strains. Also know as p-Cymene. CAS number: 99-87-6" ;
              rdfs:label "CYMENE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180929" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180930
gdsn:cv180930 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Eucalyptol is a monoterpenoid that is colourless liquid. It is found in eucalyptus trees, and several other commonly used plants such as bay leaves, cardamom, tea tree and sage. It has a vibrant fresh scent that is often described as minty and cooling. Example: a common terpene found in cannabis. Also known as cineol. CAS number: 470-82-6" ;
              rdfs:label "EUCALYPTOL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180930" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180931
gdsn:cv180931 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Fenchol is monoterpenoid and an isomer of borneol which is a colourless or white solid. It is commonly found in basil, cannabis and aster flowers. It has pine, lemon and camphor smell. Example: Fenchol is only found in high amounts in some cannabis strains. CAS number: 1632-73-1" ;
              rdfs:label "FENCHOL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180931" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180932
gdsn:cv180932 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Geranyl acetate is a monoterpene which is a colorless liquid with a pleasant floral or fruity rose aroma. It is a constituent of many essential oils, including Ceylon citronella, palmarosa, lemon grass, petit grain, neroli, geranium, coriander, carrot, Camden woollybutt, and sassafras. Example: Geranyl is present in high levels in cannabis cultivar Zkittlez, known for its fruit-forward aroma. Also known as Geranyl. CAS number: 105-87-3" ;
              rdfs:label "GERANYL_ACETATE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180932" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180933
gdsn:cv180933 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Guaiol is a sesquiterpenoid alcohol found in several plants, especially in the oil of guaiacum and cypress pine. It is known to carry a sharp woody aroma similar to pine. Example: a lesser-known cannabis terpene that tends to appear only in trace amounts. Also known as champacol. CAS number: 489-86-1" ;
              rdfs:label "GUAIOL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180933" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180934
gdsn:cv180934 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Isoborneol is an isomer of borneol terpene which occurs naturally in various plants, including nutmeg, ginger, rosemary, valerian, and fir trees. It has a spicy and woody aroma. Example: Isoborneol found in some strains of cannabis which adds a pleasant spicy-citrus or woody scent and taste to it. CAS number: 124-76-5" ;
              rdfs:label "ISOBORNEOL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180934" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180935
gdsn:cv180935 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Limonene is a monoterpene, and is the major component in the oil of citrus fruit peels such as oranges or lemons. It has a citrusy aroma. Example: Limonene is a prominent terpene found in a number of cannabis strains. CAS number: 138-86-3" ;
              rdfs:label "LIMONENE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180935" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv180936
gdsn:cv180936 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The terpene(s) has been removed from the product." ;
              rdfs:label "TERPENE_REMOVED" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "180936" ;
