###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv181696
gdsn:cv181696 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348230 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The durability index indicates the level of repairability and reliability of the product. The criteria taken into account are defined by local regulations. For example, the availability of technical documents, the ease with which the product can be dismantled, the availability of spare parts, the resistance to stress and wear, the ease of maintenance and servicing, the existence of a commercial guarantee, etc." ;
              rdfs:label "DURABILITY_INDEX" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "SustainabilityProgramCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "181696" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv181697
gdsn:cv181697 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348230 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "The repairability index indicates the level of repairability of the product. The criteria taken into account are defined by local regulations. For example, the availability of technical documents, the ease with which the product can be dismantled, the availability of spare parts, etc." ;
              rdfs:label "REPAIRABILITY_INDEX" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "SustainabilityProgramCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "181697" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv181698
gdsn:cv181698 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Beta Pinene is a bicyclic monoterpene found in plants like pine needles, rosemary and basil. It has a woody, green, pine like scent. Example: a common terpene in Cannabis. Also known as β-Pinene. CAS number: 127-91-3" ;
              rdfs:label "BETA_PINENE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "181698" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv181699
gdsn:cv181699 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Farnesene is a sesquiterpene, a type of organic compound found naturally in plants including apples, ginger, basil, grapefruit and cannabis. It is known for its sweet, woody, or fruity aroma and it is a component of various essential oils and natural coatings on fruits like apples. Example: farnesene occasionally found in small concentrations in strains with greater levels of myrcene, beta-caryophyllene, and linalool terpenes. Also known as trans-farnesene. CAS number: 502-61-4" ;
              rdfs:label "FARNESENE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "181699" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv181700
gdsn:cv181700 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Terpineol is a monoterpenoid alcohol and it is characterized by a floral, lilac like scent and can be found naturally in various plants including cardamom, cajuput oil, pine oil, and petitgrain oil. Example: a minor terpene in cannabis compared to others like humulene or caryophyllene. CAS number: 8000-41-7" ;
              rdfs:label "TERPINEOL" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "181700" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv181701
gdsn:cv181701 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Terpinolene is a terpene found in many plants, including cannabis, sage, apple, cumin, lilac, tea tree, lemon, pine and fir. It is known for its woody, floral and citrus aroma. Example: Terpinolene is more commonly found in sativa strains of cannabis, especially those with higher THC levels. Also known as alpha-terpinolene. CAS number: 58-62-9" ;
              rdfs:label "TERPINOLENE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "181701" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv181702
gdsn:cv181702 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c2147348261 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "Trans Caryophyllene is natural bicyclic sesquiterpene found in many essential oils, notably from plants used for medicinal purposes. It has a spicy, peppery and woody aroma. Example: a common terpene in cannabis and it is one of the chemical compounds that contributes to the aroma of black pepper. Also known as β-caryophyllene (BCP). CAS number: 87-44-5" ;
              rdfs:label "TRANS_CARYOPHYLLENE" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TerpeneTypeCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "181702" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv181703
gdsn:cv181703 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1329411021 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A retail channel comprising stores that specialize in home improvement, gardening, and pet-related products. This includes tools, materials, and supplies for repair, maintenance, and crafting; products for gardening, landscaping, and outdoor living; as well as food, accessories, and supplies for pets. Typical examples include hardware stores, garden centers, and pet supply retailers." ;
              rdfs:label "DIY_GARDEN_PETS" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TradeChannelCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "181703" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


###  urn:gs1:std:gdsn:cv181704
gdsn:cv181704 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       gdsn:c1329411021 ;
              dct:source "gdsn_codeValues.json" ;
              rdfs:comment "A retail channel focused on fast-moving consumer goods (FMCG), also known as consumer packaged goods (CPG) or convenience goods. These are high-turnover products sold quickly and at relatively low cost, such as packaged foods, beverages, toiletries, and household consumables. Examples include supermarkets, hypermarkets, discount retailers, and convenience stores." ;
              rdfs:label "FMCG" ;
              gdsn:codeListName "TradeChannelCode" ;
              gdsn:sourceId "181704" ;
              gdsn:sourceType "codeValue" .


